      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(7-5x)(x+1).$",
      "worked_solution": "From the equation $y=(7-5x)(x+1),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{7}{5}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{5}-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{5}-\\frac{5}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$",
